- Green and purple leaves (real fallen leaves collected from the street, plus cut green paper leaves attached to the tube);
- Red and green paper apple cutouts (a "big green apple," "red apple, you can add more green apple"), including apples on wooden sticks;
- Round green and white paper disks/circles pressed onto the cylindrical craft;
- Handwritten words and people's names added with a pen ("we can write the names of people and we can write some words on it, we can decorate it").

Note: the only explicit "Thanksgiving" mention is garbled speech ("I used to make it this Thanksgiving..."), so I can't confirm from the video that this specific craft is referred to as the "Thanksgiving tree" — but these are the decorations shown on the tree they made.
